Language English

Book Basement Ordered No Keep Looped

	Page Place
		Triggered By @PlaceBasement
		
		Prolog """
			The basement is so dark you cannot see your hand when you put it 
			through the doorway. An investigator with a light source can go
			into the basement.
		"""
		Button "Enter basement"
		
		Remove TokenExploreBasementViaDiningRoomSight
		Add TileBasement, TokenBasementWall!
		
		TEXT """
			The basement is dark, even with your light. Place the
			{c:TileBasement} tile and wall as indicated, then remove all Sight
			and Explore tokens leading to this room.
		"""
		
		exploredBasement = true
	End Page Place

	Page PlaceDarkness
		Add TokenBasementDarkness1!
		Add TokenBasementDarkness2!
		Add TokenBasementDarkness3!
		Add TokenBasementDarkness4!
		
		TEXT """
			Even with a candle, it is dark in the basement. Place Darkness in
			each space of the basement. Investigators can only move into the
			basement when a Light Source is present. The darkness feeds on your
			light:  your Light Source does not cancel the effects of darkness,
			but at least you can see into the room.
		"""
	End Page PlaceDarkness

	Page PlaceTrapdoor
		Visible When readAboutBasementDoorToCave
		
		Add TokenSearchBasementTrapdoor!
		
		Text """
			A pile of trash sits in the corner. From here, it looks like it was
			recently dumped. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page Place Trapdoor
	
	Page PlaceEvidence
		Add TokenSearchBasementEvidence!
		
		Text """
			There is more junk in one of the corners. Place a Search token as
			indicated.
		"""
		
		Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		Exit
	End Page PlaceEvidence
	
	Page SearchEvidence
		Triggered By @SearchBasementEvidence
		
		Prolog """There is a lot of refuse here."
		
		Add QItemEvidenceBasementEvidence
		Remove TokenSearchBasementEvidence
		
		Text """
			You fish through the rubbish. While you don't find anything of use,
			you do find several old pictures and a damaged necklace. One of the
			pictures shows an open door with a man walking through it. The door
			looks familiar.

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceBasementRubble} Unique Item, then discard
			this Search token.
		"""
	
		foundEvidenceBasement = true
		foundEvidenceCount = foundEvidenceCount + 1
		Exit
	End Page SearchEvidence
	
	Page SearchTrapdoor
		Triggered By @SearchBasementTrapdoor
		
		Prolog """
			The trash here is piled deep. There are footprints all around it.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenBasementWall, TokenSearchBasementTrapdoor
		
		Text """
			As you dig through the junk, you realize it is hiding something.
			You sweep it away and find a door under it. Remove this Search token
			and the wall.
		"""
	End Page SearchTrapdoor
		
	Page SearchTrapdoorExplore
		Add TokenExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement!
		
		Text """
			The door looks like it goes farther underground. Place an Explore
			token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit		
	End Page SearchTrapdoorExplore
End Book Basement